WEBVTT

00:03.000 --> 00:09.500
Welcome to this lecture on photosynthesis. Today we follow light as it is turned into sugar.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The light reactions happen in the thylakoid membranes of the chloroplast and make ATP and NADPH.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.500
Water is split in photosystem two, which releases oxygen and gives electrons to the chain.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Photosystem one passes the electrons on again and uses light to make NADPH from NADP plus.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:50.000
The Calvin cycle happens in the stroma and uses ATP and NADPH to fix carbon dioxide into sugar.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:31.500
Rubisco is the enzyme that attaches carbon dioxide to ribulose bisphosphate, the first step of the cycle.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:15.000
For every three turns of the Calvin cycle one molecule of glyceraldehyde three phosphate leaves to make sugar.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:00.000
On hot dry days the stomata close, and rubisco starts to take up oxygen instead, which is called photorespiration.
